1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:01,300
This fish swims using

2
00:00:01,350 --> 00:00:02,992
human heart cells.

3
00:00:03,042 --> 00:00:03,862
But it doesn't actually

4
00:00:03,912 --> 00:00:04,810
have a heart.

5
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:05,373
You see,

6
00:00:05,423 --> 00:00:07,140
scientists grew living heart muscle

7
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:08,024
on both sides of

8
00:00:08,074 --> 00:00:09,770
an artificial fish's tail.

9
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:11,117
When one side contracts,

10
00:00:11,167 --> 00:00:12,223
it pulls on the other,

11
00:00:12,273 --> 00:00:14,050
triggering that side to contract.

12
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,142
And this happens over and over again,

13
00:00:16,192 --> 00:00:16,966
propelling the fish

14
00:00:17,016 --> 00:00:18,032
through the water.

15
00:00:18,082 --> 00:00:19,611
It doesn't even need a motor.

16
00:00:19,661 --> 00:00:21,019
And as the cells matured,

17
00:00:21,069 --> 00:00:23,071
the fish actually got faster.

18
00:00:23,121 --> 00:00:24,562
But the scientists weren't trying

19
00:00:24,612 --> 00:00:25,911
to build a fish.

20
00:00:25,961 --> 00:00:26,878
They were figuring out

21
00:00:26,928 --> 00:00:28,739
how to build a human heart.

